+/**
+ * Packet 60 — server tells nearby clients that an explosion happened.
+ *
+ * Does not exist in vanilla a1.1.2_01. The server already runs the whole explosion
+ * (bw.a): it computes the affected blocks, damages entities and destroys terrain, and
+ * the destruction replicates because setBlockWithNotify sends block changes. What never
+ * crossed the wire was the *presentation* — the "random.explode" sound and the
+ * explode/smoke particles — so TNT and creepers detonated in complete silence with
+ * blocks quietly vanishing.
+ *
+ * Wire format is b1.7.3's (its Packet60Explosion, class `kt`): absolute double centre,
+ * float radius, then an int count followed by that many byte triples holding each
+ * affected block's offset from the *truncated* centre. Bytes are enough because the
+ * affected set never reaches 127 blocks from the centre at any survival blast radius.
+ *
+ * Server -> client only. The client must NOT re-run the explosion; it only plays the
+ * effect. See NetClientHandler.handleExplosion.
+ */
