+/**
+ * Packet 61 — play a positional sound on nearby clients.
+ *
+ * Does not exist in vanilla a1.1.2_01, and its absence is why multiplayer sounds dead:
+ * the server's only world listener (eb.java) implemented playSoundEffect as an empty
+ * method, so all 27 sound call sites in server/src fired into nothing. You could not
+ * hear another player mining, a door opening, or anything the world did — only your own
+ * actions, which your client plays locally.
+ *
+ * **Deviates from b1.7.3 on purpose.** Its packet 61 is an effect-id table
+ * (playAuxSFX(id, x, y, z, data)), which would need a translation layer for every sound
+ * alpha raises. Alpha's sound API is name-based and every call already funnels through
+ * one hook — be.a(String, double, double, double, float, float) — so carrying the name
+ * maps 1:1 onto all of them with no table to maintain. Position is sent as fixed-point
+ * eighths, matching how later Minecraft versions send their named-sound packet.
+ *
+ * Server -> client only.
+ */
+public class PacketSoundEffect extends hp {
+    public String soundName;
+    public int soundX;
+    public int soundY;
